Local change (marked LOCAL CHANGE in the source)
------------------------------------------------

`src/polyline/pline_seg_intersect.rs`, `pline_seg_intr`: when only one of the two
solutions of a line-circle or circle-circle intersection lies within both segments, an end
point lying on the other segment (within `pos_equal_eps`) replaced that solution even when
the end point belonged to the other solution, the one just outside the segment. The
crossing found was then lost, and as `find_intersects` skips intersects at a segment's end
(the next segment reports them), often nothing was reported at all: two closed loops could
be reported to cross an odd number of times. An end point now replaces the solution only
if it is nearer to it than to the other solution; otherwise both are reported.

Found with a polygonal pad whose vertex lies 9.5 nm inside a round pad's circle. Regression
tests: crates/lvp-core/tests/kernel.rs. Upstream main (2026-10-21) still has the code.
